# SHA256SUMS in this folder

`SHA256SUMS` is the checksum list from the complete frozen snapshot
`/workspace/octavo_n3_004` (376 files). Paths are relative to that snapshot
root (for example `./rust/src/lib.rs`).

This repository copy omits `lab/`, `results/`, and `attack_retest/` (lab
search trees, bench logs, and the attack-crate copy). Those lines in
`SHA256SUMS` have no matching file here. Every file that *is* present
should still match its listed hash:

```
cd n3 && grep '  \./rust/src/lib.rs$' SHA256SUMS | sha256sum -c
```

The omitted paths were left out of git on purpose; they are not a
corruption of the freeze. The full snapshot remains on the lab machine.

Octavo is still homemade; for real secrets use AES-GCM-SIV, age, or libsodium.
